index 0000000..67aed68
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/data/helix/oracle_skips.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Oracle cases that are expected to differ from Helix, one per line: <id or glob><TAB><reason>.
+# Allowed reasons: (a) indent / pairs / view tagged cases where Godot's native behaviour is intended,
+# (b) insert-mode native typing differences, (c) unicode cases needing unavailable grapheme handling.
+# The test sizes the CodeEdit to Helix's 148-row view for view-tagged cases.
+view/C-b/001	(a) view: Helix scrolls past the end of the buffer to keep scrolloff at the last line (ge); a Godot view stops at the last line, so the page up starts 4 lines higher.
+view/vgt/001	(a) view: Helix scrolls past the end of the buffer to keep scrolloff at the last line (ge); a Godot view stops at the last line, so gt lands 4 lines higher.
+insert/ret/009	(b) <ret> is native: Helix trims the whitespace before the cursor, Godot keeps it.
+insert/ret/012	(b) <ret> is native: on a whitespace-only prefix Helix moves the indent to the new line, Godot splits at the caret.
+insert/ret/015	(b) <ret> is native: Helix trims the whitespace before the cursor, Godot keeps it.
+insert/ret/016	(b) <ret> is native: Helix trims the whitespace before the cursor, Godot keeps it.
+insert/typing/006	(a) indent: native <ret> auto-indent (Godot keeps the indent and trailing whitespace).
+insert/typing/007	(b) <tab> is native: Helix's smart-tab does nothing without tree-sitter after a non-blank, Godot inserts a tab.
+insert/move/003	(b) <up> is native: on the first line Godot moves the caret to column 0, Helix stays.
+insert/move/004	(b) <down> is native: Godot keeps the pixel x position, Helix the visual column.
+insert/pairs/005	(a) pairs: native auto-brace and auto-indent between braces on <ret>.
