+# Workflow steps expected to differ from Helix, one per line: <workflow id or glob>[#<step>]<TAB><reason>.
+# A skipped step skips the rest of its workflow (the states have diverged).
+# Allowed reasons: (a) indent / pairs / view: Godot-native insert typing (Enter, Tab, auto-indent, auto-brace) or viewport size,
+# (b) other insert-mode native typing differences.
+wf/o/038#1	(a) indent: o below a line ending in an auto-indent prefix (':') adds an indent level like CodeEdit's own new line (HelixMode::_open, intended); Helix's plain-text fallback only copies the line's indent.
+wf/o/046#1	(a) indent: o below a line ending in ':' adds an indent level (CodeEdit auto-indent prefixes, intended).
+wf/native/021#1	(a) indent: o below a line ending in ':' adds an indent level (CodeEdit auto-indent prefixes, intended).
+wf/native/015#2	(a) indent: native <ret> after ':' adds an indent level (CodeEdit auto-indent).
+wf/native/018#2	(a) indent: native <ret> after ':' adds an indent level (CodeEdit auto-indent).
+wf/native/016#2	(b) <ret> is native: on a whitespace-only prefix Helix moves the indent to the new line, Godot splits at the caret (as oracle insert/ret/012).
+wf/native/017#2	(b) <ret> is native: Helix trims the whitespace before the cursor, Godot keeps it (as oracle insert/ret/009).
+wf/native/025#2	(b) <tab> is native: Helix's smart-tab does nothing without tree-sitter after a non-blank, Godot inserts a tab (as oracle insert/typing/007).
+wf/native/026#2	(b) <tab> is native: Helix's smart-tab does nothing without tree-sitter after a non-blank, Godot inserts a tab (as oracle insert/typing/007).
+wf/bol/061#2	(a) indent: native <backspace> in space indentation of a tab-indented buffer removes one space (CodeEdit unindents to the indent stop only with indent_using_spaces); Helix goes back to the previous indent stop.
+wf/bol/062#2	(a) indent: native <backspace> in space indentation of a tab-indented buffer removes one space (CodeEdit unindents to the indent stop only with indent_using_spaces); Helix goes back to the previous indent stop.
